From 2eefe69e5d6796e3bbfd35b4be5130b7dc7b767c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:43:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(3d): facet grid for the drop-cutter support scan

The support facets of 3D finishing are now a SupSet: the facets plus a
uniform XY bucket grid (CSR cells, Ericson ch. 7). The point scans
(support_at, support_grad, ball_clear, column_clear, fold_best) read only
the facets of the cell that holds the query point. Each scan keeps its
own padded-box reject, and each cell lists its facets in ascending index,
so every answer has the same bits as the full scan.

A non-finite box, a non-finite query or an extent that the grid cannot
size falls back to the full scan. SupSet::full_scan keeps the old scan as
the reference for the parity tests and for the GPU filter of #2526.

Pinned by grid_scan_matches_full_scan_on_bumps,
grid_scan_matches_full_scan_on_big_and_degenerate_facets,
grid_candidates_hold_every_facet_whose_box_holds_the_point and
non_finite_input_falls_back_to_the_full_scan.

Fixes #2619

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
